{"chunk_id":"R5-231989-header","collection":"ran5_cr_chunks","metadata":{"source":"","specNumber":"34.229-1","tdocNumber":"R5-231989","title":"Correction to PIDF Location object contents"},"point_id":"12312580625552921330"}
Title: Correction to PIDF Location object contents Reason for change: The Rel-15 core specification (TS 24.229) requirement PIDF-LO structure is in accordance to RFC 4119 while in later releases (Rel-16 and beyond) RFC 5491 is added along with RFC 4119 for PIDF-LO structure. RFC 5491 includes optional “device” and “person” types as containers for geopriv-info alongside “tuple” defined in RFC 4119 & 3863. Summary of change: A note added in UPDATE (Step 7) specific message contents in test case 19.3.1 and in clause A.2.1 to clarify that UE may send PIDF-LO element using the RFC 4119 or 5491 In addition Content-Type of the PIDF document ("application/pidf+xml") is added to the MIME body, more then one location element may be contained in a <geopriv> element and presence of the <usage-rules> is not needed as it is mandatory according to the XML schema. Consequences if not approved: A conformant device mail fail the test case Clauses affected: 19.3.1, A.2.1

